Skip NodePort SNAT conflict handling for host traffic to a local endpoint.

The hunks of https://github.com/cilium/cilium/pull/49232 (commit
e0462275b8164463ae9b473b32718a64645cda6d), verbatim, applied to cilium
v1.20.2 bpf/lib/nodeport_egress.h. Upstream commit 990f79be17
("bpf,nodeport: generalize SNAT conflict detection") runs the conflict path
for any host-marked packet on every bpf_host device, and that path replaces
MARK_MAGIC_HOST with MARK_MAGIC_SNAT_DONE. With kube-ovn chaining, host
traffic to a local pod leaves through ovn0, so the pod sees it as world:
kubelet probes fail under default-deny ingress policies and a world deny
drops the API server calling a webhook on its own node. Upstream report:
https://github.com/cilium/cilium/issues/49208, downstream tracking:
https://github.com/cozystack/cozystack/issues/4781.

Drop this patch once a cilium release we ship carries cilium/cilium#49232.
Until then `make update` dry-runs it against the new tag.

--- a/lib/nodeport_egress.h
+++ b/lib/nodeport_egress.h
@@ -46,6 +46,10 @@
 	 * already reserved.
 	 */
 	if (magic == MARK_MAGIC_HOST || (ep && (ep->flags & ENDPOINT_F_HOST))) {
+		/* See comment in nodeport_has_nat_conflict_ipv4(). */
+		if (__lookup_ip6_endpoint((union v6addr *)&ip6->daddr))
+			return false;
+
 		ipv6_addr_copy(&target->addr, (union v6addr *)&ip6->saddr);
 		target->needs_ct = true;
 		return true;
@@ -314,6 +318,15 @@
 	 * already reserved.
 	 */
 	if (magic == MARK_MAGIC_HOST || (ep && (ep->flags & ENDPOINT_F_HOST))) {
+		/* Host traffic to a local endpoint never leaves the node, so it
+		 * cannot collide with egress SNAT and must keep MARK_MAGIC_HOST.
+		 * The SNAT path would replace that mark with MARK_MAGIC_SNAT_DONE,
+		 * and with CNI chaining the destination endpoint would then see
+		 * the source as world.
+		 */
+		if (__lookup_ip4_endpoint(ip4->daddr))
+			return false;
+
 		target->addr = ip4->saddr;
 		target->needs_ct = true;
 		return true;
